{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>et the pillar of cloud.</b> The word את is attached to the verb; it is \"the pillar\" that did not depart from them. And generally it [את] comes with the verb, except for this, and a few others with it, such as ואת מלכנו שרינו כהנינו ואבותינו לא עשו תורתך (and our kings, our officers, our priests, and our fathers did not keep your Torah). And the lion came ואת הדוב ונשא שה (and the bear, and carried off a sheep)." "<b>on the way.</b> Correctly comes with the heh of the definite article."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The last phrase weaves together two examples: one from Nehemiah 9:34 itself, and the bear-lion-sheep illustration of the unusual את construction."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:31.304603787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}